Facility and personnel requirements for hub zoos and hub aquariums (related to Article 22(3))

1. Hub zoos

  a. Facility requirements
    1) A total area of at least 10,000 square meters.
    2) A veterinary hospital under Article 2(4) of the Veterinarians Act, which must include consultation, examination, treatment, and inpatient rooms.
    3) Classrooms and on-site training areas.
    4) Research and experimental facilities and training facilities for trial releases.
    5) Quarantine facilities: isolation quarantine areas and facilities capable of directly diagnosing diseases.
    6) Veterinary equipment: an ultrasound diagnostic device, centrifuge, bacterial incubator, gastroscope, polymerase chain reaction (PCR) testing device, and enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) diagnostic device.
  b. Personnel requirements
    1) Operations and management personnel: at least five persons in total.
    2) Husbandry and welfare personnel: at least eight persons in total.
    3) Facility and landscaping personnel: at least two persons in total.
    4) Veterinary personnel: at least four persons in total, comprising at least three veterinarians and at least one person assisting with veterinary work.

2. Hub aquariums

  a. Facility requirements
    1) A tank floor area of at least 10,000 square meters or a total tank capacity of at least 5,000 cubic meters.
    2) An institution designated both as an ex situ conservation institution under Article 17 of the Conservation and Management of Marine Ecosystems Act and as a specialized institution for marine animal rescue and treatment under Article 18 of that Act.
    3) Classrooms and on-site training areas.
    4) Research and experimental facilities and experimental tank facilities.
    5) Quarantine facilities: isolation quarantine areas and facilities capable of directly diagnosing diseases.
    6) Veterinary equipment: an ultrasound diagnostic device, centrifuge, bacterial incubator, gastroscope, and blood testing device.
  b. Personnel requirements
    1) Operations and management personnel: at least five persons in total.
    2) Husbandry and welfare personnel: at least eight persons in total.
    3) Facility and water quality management personnel: at least two persons in total.
    4) Veterinary personnel: at least four persons in total, comprising at least two veterinarians, including at least one full-time veterinarian, and at least two aquatic organism disease inspectors.

